# The latch reads `setp.lt.u32` of -4 as unsigned, 2^32 - 4, its counter
# counting from 1 and so never negative; the loop runs 2^32 - 4 trips
# (ptxas 13.4: `ISETP.GE.U32 ... -0x4`, `@!P0 BRA`; an RTX 4090 run
# stores 4294967292). The guard reads the same
# comparison of %tid.x as unsigned, true on every thread. A signed
# latch reads 0xFFFFFFFF as its `.s32` value, -1, so the loop runs one
# trip (ptxas 13.4: `ISETP.GE.AND ... -0x1`; the RTX 4090 run stores 1).
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/latch_unsigned.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
ANN: {{^}}$L__BB0_1: // loop: trips 4294967292 | warp * × lane * | exec 137,438,953,344/CTA{{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd1], %r1; // [<block 1>] warp * × lane * | exec 32/CTA | global store [param_0] sectors/req 1 (ideal 1){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}$L__BB2_1: // loop: trips 1 | global per CTA: requested 4 B, unique 4 B, sectors 32 B | warp * × lane * | exec 1/CTA{{$}}
